<<<
data is plural only (The d. are, not 2s, insufficient./What are the d.?/We have no d.); the singular, comparatively rare, is datum; one of the data is commoner than a datum; but datum-line, line taken as a basis, is common.
===
**data** is plural only (*The d. are, not is, insufficient./What are the d.?/We have no d.*); the singular, comparatively rare, is *datum*; *one of the data* is commoner than *a datum*; but *datum-line*, line taken as a basis, is common.
>>>

<<<
My Intelligence Department has furnished me with so much valuable data illustrates the mistake of taking the plural for a singular.
===
*My Intelligence Department has furnished me with so much valuable data* illustrates the mistake of taking the plural for a singular.
>>>

<<<
date. For d., epoch, &c., see TIME.
===
**date.** For *d., epoch*, &c., see ^^TIME^^.
>>>
